  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Smile Again Family Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Smile Again family project would like to see teenage mothers who have unveiled their hidden potential, are able to stand-up for their rights, taking-up leadership roles in their communities, reaching their desired childhood dreams.

Our main objective in this project is to empower Teenage Mothers with foundational life and entrepreneurial skills needed for them to start and sustainably run micro &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; small Income Generating Activities for self-sustenance.

We will give them a voice by empowering them with English hope based language and ICT literacy, for them to be able to gain confidence to stand up and speak for themselves and others. Support them to learn to read and write given information as well as introduce them to use ICT skills to acquire knowledge and share information that is pertinent to themselves. This is to support them break the barriers that inhibit them to exercise their right of speech and be heard by concerned authorities.

Secondly we shall train them in foundational life skills that will encompass, self-esteem, human rights and reproductive health rights for advocacy.

Thirdly, Train them in leadership skills, to empower them to take up leadership roles in their communities.

Lastly to train, mentor and support 50 teenage mothers to innovatively ideate startup and or strengthen micro and small income generating activities.  This will be done through group training, one on one mentorship and coaching.

Project Goal
To empower 50 teenage mothersto know and advocate for theirhuman rights and own sustainable businesses to achieve economic independence.

Project Title
Empowered teenage mothers,living their full potential.

Specifically, the objectives of the project are;
&#x2022; To train 50 teenage mothers to speak and write English and computer literacy for them to communicate their issues to the world around them.

&#x2022; Empower 50 teenage mothers with foundational life skills, to grow in self-esteem, knowing their rights, and advocating for them.

&#x2022; To train 50 teenage mothers in leadership skills and place them in solidarity groups to enhance a sense of belonging, support and continued community engagement.

&#x2022; To support 50 teenage mothers identify and implement viable businesses and mentorthem manage their enterprises effectively.</narrative>
  </description>
