   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SMILE AGAIN FAMILY PROJECT</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Smile Again Family Project exists :
To empower teenage mothers with foundational life and entrepreneurial skills needed for them toknow and advocate for their human rights and own sustainable businesses to achieve economic independence.
&#x2022; To promote respect for human rights of women and girls for their meaningful participation in development.
&#x2022; To empower women and girls to demand for economic, sexual reproductive health rights for improved livelihoods.
&#x2022; To improve women and girl&#x2019;s access to specialized maternal and child health services for improved quality of life.

The organisation works with a board of governance which influence the policies, strategic plan and  standards of  operations documents. These inform how all decisions are arrived at. The organisation Human resourcepolicy informs how we recruit staff and the board charter defines how we select the board and how often the board meetings should be held. The finance and procurement policies guide us on acquisition of assets , cash and expense management.

The organisation works with other social actors like the District Health Officer who supervises the work we do and sits on the organisation board, the Community Development officer who also checks the activities of the organisation ,Masaka City NGO forum which checks the operation of the organisation especially the structure and functionality. The church and local leaders in the communities we work in especially in identifying the rights holders that need the organisation support.

The staff  are passionate about the work that they do and theyensure protection of the rights and wellbeing of the rights holders. The staff believe in the rights holders and know that no matter what the y have gone through they can become great changemakers as long as they discover their inner worth and life purpose.</narrative>
